ome/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D3/3/code.py:103:    Tile one transformed/scaled patch across a quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D3/3/code.py:145:    Replicate a motif across quadrants, then tile the transformed motif through each target quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D3/3/code.py:160:      the aligned transformed motif becomes a tile that repeats across the entire target quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/1/code.py:46:    - The asymmetry is repeated across every frame in one sample, so the eye can detect a consistent rectangular cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/1/code.py:64:    - Across samples, the generator varies between (tb,lr)=(1,2) and (2,1), so the rule cannot be reduced to the old fixed +1 inset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:22:#    D5 is also flipped: when two colors claim the same crossing, the currently more complete color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:27:#    two-stage cascade and at least one crossing where complete-first and fragmented-first disagree.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:28:#    The family is kept narrow on purpose: a vertical backbone crosses two horizontal lines, which is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:29:#    enough repetition for humans to see both the iterative fill and the reversed crossing preference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:38:#    conflicts other than intended crossings. Marker cells are isolated singletons, stay in-bounds, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:45:#    unless complete-first changes at least one crossing relative to fragmented-first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:47:#    The scene is intentionally sparse: three one-cell-thick lines, two crossings, and two isolated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/