ans plus\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D2/2/code.py:103:- The generator therefore switches to input-first construction:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D17/1/code.py:38:    - mixed directions introduce ordering risk, so the solver switches to repeated one-step simulation with fixed per-yellow directions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/4/code.py:54:#    - Samples always contain multiple frames, at least one cross-frame shared shape, and every frame's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/4/code.py:228:    - The puzzle is still driven by shape-coded color lookup, but now the lookup table is shared across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/62593bfd/D14/1/code.py:54:#    - Across examples, the user will see a few tiny colored dots vanish while the larger shapes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D1/2/code.py:22:#       prototype identity across the row boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D1/2/code.py:49:#     - Only two prototype identities exist, repeated across the four sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D1/2/code.py:141:    - The grouping cue is spatial rather than chromatic: prototype exchange happens across the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/62593bfd/D10/0/code.py:45:    - find_components(..., monochromatic=False, connectivity=8) merges touching objects even across colors, so generator must forbid 8-neighbor contact, not just overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D1/4/code.py:416:    # Prefer 6-12 pieces so the complement evidence repeats across multiple joins.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/5/code.py:75:#    - Across a few examples, a human can see that the number of true matching sprites\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/5/code.py:549:    \"\"\"Pick 3-5 unique near-miss shapes distributed across real bases when possible.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/28/code.py:29:#   Step 3 is the 