ed anchor-colored family swaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D6/1/code.py:21:#    repeated across all sprites and across both structural families, so 2-4 examples are enough for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D6/1/code.py:44:#    Only three variable colors participate in the cycle. They appear repeatedly across all sprites and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D6/1/code.py:132:    - The output does not switch a sprite into the other structural family anymore. The only change is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D19/1/code.py:45:# - The sprite template stays shared across frames so the task still looks like\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D19/1/code.py:298:      background is the most common color across the full grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D10/2/code.py:28:#    - Each sprite gets an ordered pair of colors with no reuse across sprites, so humans can track\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D10/2/code.py:112:    - Geometry is shared across all sprites, so the only thing that circulates is the full color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D10/2/code.py:280:    \"\"\"Pick count ordered color pairs with no reuse across sprites.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D17/1/code.py:21:#    The role system stays small and repeated across every sample: red = move, green =\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D17/1/code.py:37:#    The generator enforces total input sprites across all four lanes <= 6, so the green\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D17/1/code.py:44:#    of donor, but the copy batch is separated upward from the moved batch. Across a few\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D14/0/code.py:27:  equally sized across the two prototypes; the generator keeps that invariant. The new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D14/0/code.py:36:  This prevents overlap, clipping, and cross-sprite interference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/