/D1/2/code.py:326:        cross = w if long_is_rows else h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:327:        cross_max = short_dim - cross - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:328:        if cross_max < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:330:        cross0 = random.randint(1, cross_max)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:334:            new_item[\"c\"] = int(cross0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:337:            new_item[\"r\"] = int(cross0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D7/1/code.py:69:    - If the translated sprite would cross the old frame, expand the output grid on that side instead of clipping it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/0/code.py:90:    - Horizontal red line => reflect across that row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/0/code.py:91:    - Vertical red line => reflect across that column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/1/code.py:52:#    bottommost cell of the border run, the relation is consistent across examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D15/0/code.py:37:#      This keeps the task inferable from a few examples instead of branching across many\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D15/0/code.py:56:#    - Across examples, both input connectors visibly sit on the same side of their bodies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D7/2/code.py:48:#       per sample, but still varies that edge across samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D5/0/code.py:249:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D15/2/code.py:28:#   The bar length still has only 1-3 choices and must match across sprites, which keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D15/1/code.py:292:    Continue a marker-consuming arrow simulation whose sprite template alternates across snapshots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/