ove/left of the base.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D13/1/code.py:68:#      the merged bodies cross; every generated example contains at least one red\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D13/1/code.py:72:#    - Only one extra layer of meaning is added: red marks crossings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D12/3/code.py:30:#    The allowed spans are restricted to 3..5 and each puzzle reuses 2-3 span values across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/_variant_lib.py:195:def _layout_cross_hub() -> Layout:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/_variant_lib.py:379:        return _layout_cross_hub()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D7/0/code.py:60:# - Across examples, the merged shape is the same as the original task, but the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/0/code.py:46:#    The marker color varies across samples and is not red. In many samples red is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D9/1/code.py:243:    Paint each walled-off region with a cyclic frame pattern, then let the center color spill across walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D9/1/code.py:251:    - Second, inspect the finished first-pass picture: each region's deepest layer color crosses any shared wall and overwrites the neighboring region's wall-adjacent outer layer by one cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D9/1/code.py:279:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/2/code.py:56:#    Across 2-4 examples a human should see two linked effects: bars are reordered by height\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:45:#   sprite lookup code must switch from color-keyed matching to shape-keyed recolor + target-keyed placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/1/code.py:139:    - Red (2) singleton embedded in a component means: reflect payload across that pixel's row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/1/code.py:140:    - Blue (1) singleton embedded in a component means: reflect payload across that pixel's column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D7/2/code.py:59:#     - Across examples, the solver still clearly \"moves plug onto base\", but the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/4/code.py:16:#   several same-width monochrome vertical bars that cross the baseline and have\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/4/code.py:62:#   Across examples, the input visibly shows different bar heights and shuffled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/4/code.py:69:#     identical across rows. The generator guarantees that by drawing solid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:11:#     new_hub: 6x6 thick cross made from five 2x2 blocks:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:20:#       - C is a fifth neutral hub-center color used only to keep the cross 4-connected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:27:#       - mirror symmetry across the contact axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:36:#   structural/positional: square perimeter -> radial cross arms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:40:# - The neutral 2x2 center is necessary; without it the four arm colors cannot form one connected cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:48:# These are replaced by an explicit 6x6 cross detector and four arm-tip contact specs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:54:# - The cross occupies 20 cells inside a 6x6 bbox and has four empty 2x2 corners, so it is visually\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:58:# - Exactly one near-center 6x6 thick cross exists.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:152:def _find_cross_hub(g: np.ndarray, bg: int):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:157:            # The four 2x2 corners must be background so the 6x6 bbox visibly reads as a cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:232:    hub = _find_cross_hub(g, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/0/code.py:230:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/3/code.py:146:    - Mirror the whole sprite across that axis. Originals and red controls remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:13:#       Each target is an interior crosshair:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:15:#       - one short perpendicular tick crossing the rail,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:16:#       - a colored center pixel at the crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:33:#       A horizontal rail on row 6 with crosshair center at (6, 9) means the marker must end\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:36:#       so the generator switches to one sprite per crosshair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:46:#       shared orientation. The dataset still varies orientation across samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:50:#       - \"anchor is an isolated singleton\": false now, because the center is embedded in a crosshair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:72:#       - crosshair centers as the destinations,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:78:#     That avoids clutter near the rails and keeps the new crosshair cue unambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:92:    Slide multi-color sprites along interior crosshair rails until their marker pixels reach the matching centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:96:    - One or more interior crosshairs: a long monochrome rail plus a short perpendicular tick, with a colored center pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:97:    - Multi-color sprites whose minori