snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D17/0/code.py:34:#    - The human sees the same cross seed plus a few red blockers. In the output the red blockers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D17/0/code.py:38:#    - Obstacles are isolated and kept away from the cross center, so the grid remains legible. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D17/0/code.py:65:    Grow four clockwise spiral paths from a teal cross while red blockers stay fixed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D17/0/code.py:68:    - bg = 0 (black). One teal (8) plus-sign cross with a center hole, plus several red (2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D17/0/code.py:79:    miniature walls. The solver therefore identifies the cross exactly as before, runs the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D8/2/code.py:37:#   Every generated sample contains at least one marker type repeated across all\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D8/2/code.py:179:    - Shape identity and paint color are now split across two cues: marker hue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D1/1/code.py:273:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D1/1/code.py:413:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:17:#     new: the diagonal connector still behaves the same, but every trigger now emits a 4-way orthogonal cross:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:55:#     - branch direction is obvious from 2-3 examples because magenta expands in axis-aligned crosses rather than diagonals\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:57:#     - cross rays are prevented from overlapping earlier diagonals/rays during generation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:71:    Connect same-color diagonal endpoint pairs, then emit orthogonal cross rays from trigger pixels on those diagonals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:81:    - The diagonal backbone 